<p>A new <%= kind === 'issue' ? 'issue report' : 'contact message' %> arrived on <%= appName %>.</p>
<table style="font-size:14px;border-collapse:collapse">
  <tr><td style="padding:2px 12px 2px 0;color:#6b7280">From</td><td><%= name %> &lt;<%= fromEmail %>&gt;</td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:2px 12px 2px 0;color:#6b7280">Subject</td><td><%= subject %></td></tr>
</table>
<%#
  The message itself is included so that somebody reading on a phone can triage without
  opening anything. It is escaped like every other value here — a message body is plain
  text, and the one thing it must never do is become markup in our own inbox.
%>
<p style="margin:16px 0;padding:12px;background:#f3f4f6;border-radius:8px;white-space:pre-wrap"><%= body %></p>
<p style="margin:24px 0">
  <a href="<%= reviewUrl %>"
     style="background:#0b5cab;color:#ffffff;padding:12px 22px;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;display:inline-block">
    Open it in the queue
  </a>
</p>
<p style="font-size:13px;color:#6b7280">
  Reply to the address above, not to this message. The queue is the record of what was
  asked; this is only the nudge towards it.
</p>
